<title>TURKEY: TURK GARANTIBANK H1 NET PROFIT JUMPS.</title>
<headline>TURK GARANTIBANK H1 NET PROFIT JUMPS.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>					 H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>					 -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	634.69  vs     390.67</p>
<p>    Net profit		    25,387.15  vs   7,031.97</p>
<p>    Net interest income	 50,732.62  vs  16,661.33</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense  20,320.58  vs   8,977.14</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans   4,229.3   vs	0</p>
<p>    Loans extended	     360,859.03  vs 132,040.99</p>
<p>    Deposits		     282,896.86  vs 127,734.52</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed	     241,732.54  vs  71,016.17</p>
<p>    Equity			  60,028.91  vs  25,162.01</p>
<p>    Capital			 40,000.00  vs  18,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Garanti Bankasi AS, whose shares are also listed on the London Stock Exchange in the form of ADSs, is largely owned by Turkish construction and finance group Dogus Holding AS.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
